# Copy to .env, which `bench` loads from the working directory or a parent. The endpoint serves
# OpenAI APIs and native Anthropic Messages. Each base is configured independently. The key and
# optional CA bundle are read from files, so no secret is
# copied into the checkout. BENCH_API_HEADERS takes a JSON object of extra request headers.
# BENCH_API_LOCAL_ADDRESS binds outgoing connections to a local address, such as 0.0.0.0 for IPv4,
# and a bound client connects directly, ignoring the proxy variables.
BENCH_API_BASE_URL=https://api.example.com/v1
BENCH_ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=https://api.example.com/anthropic
BENCH_API_KEY_FILE=/path/to/api-key
BENCH_API_CA_FILE=
BENCH_API_HEADERS=
BENCH_API_LOCAL_ADDRESS=
